From 394a1b498c32e2e636cd3a875ac5b2446508e319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 245/248] Bugfix: do not overwrite earlier errors with the
 numbering hole error in `dgraphCheck()`

When an edge end lies in a numbering hole of a neighbor process,
`dgraphCheck()` unconditionally set the local error code to 4, thus
overwriting an error (1 to 3) already found on the same process. The
check result is unaffected, but the reported message was misleading
("arc end in numbering hole" instead of "arc data do not match").

Only set the hole error code when no error has been found yet.

Tested with a 2-process reproducer (unmatched arc followed by an arc
end in a hole, on each process): the message was "arc end in numbering
hole" before, "arc data do not match" after. test_scotch_dgraph_check
on bump.grf at np=1 and np=3 with ASan/UBSan: passes; dgraph_check.c
compiles without warning with -Wall.
---
 src/libscotch/dgraph_check.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/dgraph_check.c b/src/libscotch/dgraph_check.c
index bf3e580..7a15504 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/dgraph_check.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/dgraph_check.c
@@ -471,7 +471,8 @@ fail:
           Gnum                edgengbsum;
 
           if (vertglbend >= vertngbnnd) {         /* If end vertex lies in numbering hole of neighbor process */
-            cheklocval = 4;
+            if (cheklocval == 0)                  /* Do not overwrite an error already found */
+              cheklocval = 4;
             continue;
           }
           for (edgengbnum = vertngbptr[vertglbend - vertngbmin],
